    {
      "id": "claim_542bc73c42bb43fdb87c61258bc4e252",
      "statement": "_content_duplicate_fraction excludes both short lines and lines occurring more than a small number of times before measuring repetition, so page headers and footers repeated across a long PDF are treated as structural boilerplate rather than duplicated content — a test confirms a header repeated five times alongside one unique paragraph yields exactly 0.0.",
